0..79 Comment "// A wheel in a `theory` block: a rule whose output feeds back, one step later,"
80..159 Comment "// as a port its own body reads. The fed-back port is read under an observation"
160..226 Comment "// of its sort, one tick, so the loop is guarded; the bare twin is"
227..303 Comment "// `pathological/circuit/circuit-feed-wheel.gandr` (#1031). Feedback follows"
304..380 Comment "// Katis, Sabadini and Walters (_Feedback, Trace and Fixed-Point Semantics_,"
381..454 Comment "// RAIRO-ITA 36(2), 2002, doi:10.1051/ita:2002009); the guard follows the"
455..529 Comment "// feedback rule of Di Lavore, de Felice and Román (_Monoidal Streams for"
530..596 Comment "// Dataflow Programming_, LICS 2022, doi:10.1145/3531130.3533365)."
598..670 Comment "/// A running fold: each step reads the stream\'s value together with the"
671..748 Comment "/// previous output through the observation `emit`, and feeds its output back"
749..798 Comment "/// as `state`. The block binds `Wheel : Theory`."
